examples.solution_text:
Label equal vertical steps $0,4,8,12,16,20$. Divide each count by $4$ to find the number of steps.

Dog: $12\div4=3$ steps. Cat: $20\div4=5$ steps. Rabbit: $0\div4=0$ steps. Fish: $16\div4=4$ steps.

Draw equal-width columns with equal gaps. Keep Rabbit on the axis with no visible column height.

[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[x=1cm,y=0.65cm,every node/.style={font=\fontsize{10}{12}\selectfont,text=black},draw=black]
\foreach \y in {1,...,5} {\draw[draw=gray!40] (0,\y)--(8,\y);}
\draw[->] (0,0)--(0,5.6);
\draw[->] (0,0)--(8.3,0);
\foreach \y/\v in {0/0,1/4,2/8,3/12,4/16,5/20} {\draw (-0.1,\y)--(0,\y);\node[left,font=\fontsize{8.5}{10}\selectfont] at (-0.1,\y) {\v};}
\draw (0.5,0) rectangle (1.5,3);
\draw (2.5,0) rectangle (3.5,5);
\draw (6.5,0) rectangle (7.5,4);
\foreach \x/\name in {1/Dog,3/Cat,5/Rabbit,7/Fish} {\node[below] at (\x,0) {\name};}
\node[above] at (4,5.8) {Pets owned by students};
\node[rotate=90] at (-1,2.5) {Number of students};
\node at (4,-1.1) {Pet};
\node[above] at (1,3) {12};
\node[above] at (3,5) {20};
\node[above] at (5,0) {0};
\node[above] at (7,4) {16};
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]

