examples.question_text:
A library has $18$ Adventure books, $30$ Mystery books and $24$ Fantasy books. A student draws the graph below.

Identify and correct both incorrect columns.

[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[x=1.2cm,y=0.65cm,every node/.style={font=\fontsize{10}{12}\selectfont,text=black},draw=black]
\foreach \y in {1,...,5} {\draw[draw=gray!40] (0,\y)--(6,\y);}
\draw[->] (0,0)--(0,5.6);
\draw[->] (0,0)--(6.3,0);
\foreach \y/\v in {0/0,1/6,2/12,3/18,4/24,5/30} {\draw (-0.1,\y)--(0,\y);\node[left,font=\fontsize{8.5}{10}\selectfont] at (-0.1,\y) {\v};}
\draw (0.5,0) rectangle (1.5,3);
\draw (2.5,0) rectangle (3.5,4);
\draw (4.5,0) rectangle (5.5,3.5);
\foreach \x/\name in {1/Adventure,3/Mystery,5/Fantasy} {\node[below] at (\x,0) {\name};}
\node[above] at (3,5.8) {Library books};
\node[rotate=90] at (-1,2.5) {Number of books};
\node at (3,-1.1) {Genre};
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]

examples.solution_text:
The Mystery column reaches $24$, but its count is $30$. Raise it by one step of $6$ to the label $30$.

The Fantasy column ends halfway between $18$ and $24$. Its count is $24$, so raise its top to the tick labelled $24$.

The Adventure column already reaches its count of $18$.

[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[x=1.2cm,y=0.65cm,every node/.style={font=\fontsize{10}{12}\selectfont,text=black},draw=black]
\foreach \y in {1,...,5} {\draw[draw=gray!40] (0,\y)--(6,\y);}
\draw[->] (0,0)--(0,5.6);
\draw[->] (0,0)--(6.3,0);
\foreach \y/\v in {0/0,1/6,2/12,3/18,4/24,5/30} {\draw (-0.1,\y)--(0,\y);\node[left,font=\fontsize{8.5}{10}\selectfont] at (-0.1,\y) {\v};}
\draw (0.5,0) rectangle (1.5,3);
\draw (2.5,0) rectangle (3.5,5);
\draw (4.5,0) rectangle (5.5,4);
\foreach \x/\name in {1/Adventure,3/Mystery,5/Fantasy} {\node[below] at (\x,0) {\name};}
\node[above] at (3,5.8) {Library books};
\node[rotate=90] at (-1,2.5) {Number of books};
\node at (3,-1.1) {Genre};
\node[above] at (1,3) {18};
\node[above] at (3,5) {30};
\node[above] at (5,4) {24};
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]
